IDS=['eye-of-judgement']
Q=[
('EYE1-Q01',IDS,'Source Action60rank6WIS, reveal/suppress class features1round; prior failed-save snapshot then suppression.','A: save before changing any defenses, success negates both, failure resolves reading with pre-suppression protections then applies separate suppression. B: strip a defense first to bootstrap the read.','Recommend A. Current source-qualified information defenses can block only the reading while whole-spell protection blocks both. No secret class roster is learned from a blocked read or by rerunning after its defense disappears. Counterspell and actual reactions at cast windows happen before the suppressed state exists.'),
('EYE1-Q02',IDS,'One round does not specify initiative endpoint; prior first future target regularEND excluding an in-progress turn, or six seconds outside.','A: retain explicit proposed target-marker rule, no concentration/repeat save, extra turns excluded. B: source-nextSTART or exact six-second duration.','Request explicit local choice and transition rules. OptionA can last nearly two target-turn intervals when applied during its current turn; state that consequence honestly. Preserve a fixed virtual marker across absence/initiative changes, and expiry ordering. No duration refresh from suppression/resumption.'),
('EYE1-Q03',IDS,'Reveal actual class features, not every statistic, lore or unselected future path.','A: actual acquired Base/Arch/Hero/Mystery/Oath mechanics and necessary class identity, snapshot only. B: full character sheet, resources, prepared spells, biography or unpublished NPC class.','Recommend A. An empty classified roster differs from missing/unclassified records; use explicit Indeterminate without invented stats. Disclosure of a feature’s actual operative formula can support ordinary level/ability inference but grants no independent hidden-field query. Does the exact numeric acquired mode/configuration need disclosure where formula alone is insufficient? Decide boundedly.'),
('EYE1-Q04',IDS,'Oracle intrinsic Curse protection and Oracle’sBurden/card8 cannot be bypassed by generic suspension; Soul-CrackedBoonIV/card46 gives direct-divination d2 symbolic output.','A: preserve selected intrinsic Curse/expressly protected effects and original information defense timing, including true engine/acquisition prerequisites. B: suppress Burden first then treat Curse as ordinary removable class feature.','A is required inherited boundary. Do not invent random false class data, permanent cure or soul mechanics. Separate BoonIV direct-divination result from its +2 mind-control-save benefit: Eye is class suppression, so no automatic mind-control classification merely from WIS. Account for level1 intrinsic limitation versus actual level2Burden acquisition.'),
('EYE1-Q05',IDS,'All17classes contain engines, cards, automatic progressions, class skills, permanent ASIs, feats and native NPC actions.','A: suppress continuing class-feature permissions/modifiers but retain earned levels, ordinary PB/baseHP/baseRP schedule, permanent ASIs, ordinary training, independent feats/ancestry/items/native actions. B: erase whole sheet or allow duplicate engine/card alias to survive.','Recommend A with a full classification table and source precedence. True class expertise multiplier is suppressed while ordinary proficiency persists; a feat acquired throughASI stays a feat. Underlying ordinaryAction remains; losing preferred options is not automatic full-Action denial or new hard-control admission.'),
('EYE1-Q06',IDS,'Old class cast versus independent spell application, prepared Ready cast, continuous modifier and pending class activation differ.','A: existing ordinary spells retain own life/concentration, actual continuing class modifiers cease; genuinely class-maintained effects are inoperative. B: suppress all earlier spells merely because a class cast them.','Recommend A but resolve actual already-paid Readyspell release separately from suppressed new-casting permission, and actual class technique commitment separately from ordinary projectile. No refund/free release or extra Counterspell window. Costs, Refrain, Dissonance, recovery and all spent histories persist; nonclass surviving permissions must be real full sources.'),
('EYE1-Q07',IDS,'Form anatomy is class-maintained; reviewed body/meld rules distinguish suppression from final reversion.','A: explicit Eye-local class-form suppression through one-body/root normalization with retained inaccessible original meld and original clock; only still-legal resume. B: treat suppression as paid fresh shift, gear retrieval window or automatic move to surface.','Recommend A as a required new application to actual Druid forms, not an assumed general spell rule. Preserve transformed body weight, external items, no-hand anatomy, ownHP and form-specific concentration. Unsupported root falls normally; blocked root uses adjacent same-region conflict, no remote rescue. Resume grants no new buffer/FormSurge/Refrain-reset trigger.'),
('EYE1-Q08',IDS,'Class-created companions/devices and ordinary spell-created bodies have distinct command/ownership dependencies.','A: retain physical body/slot/cargo/currentHP; suspend only actual class authority and continuous modifier outputs; source-specific defensive/native agency retains original phase. B: dissolve all bodies, grant autonomous offense or rerun creation.','Recommend A with actual Wizard/Ranger/Mirrorsage/Tinker distinctions. Existing source-independent spell command permission may survive only if actually provided. Pending orders dependent on suppressed class permission need exact execution/loss policy. No duplicate phase, fresh source slot or offturn offense. Unaccepted companion Current04 is a comparison only.'),
('EYE1-Q09',IDS,'MaximumHP ledger has nonhealing downward clamp; created Conjuration amount is snapshotted while FleshAscendant is controller-dynamic.','A: suppress still-class-dependent maxHP bonuses even on remote dependents while preserving their recorded amount and independent sources. B: freeze every creation bonus as permanently independent or refill HP on return.','Recommend A only with explicit exact-dependency classification, avoiding snapshot-versus-continuing-authority confusion. Recompute max from separate records, clamp normalHP without damage/Wounds/triggers; tempHP independent; restoration noHP. Original base60+20/75→60→max80HP60 is an arithmetic obligation until a legal complete actual class fixture is supplied.'),
('EYE1-Q10',IDS,'Prior new inaccessible resource reserve avoids deleting over-cap units; accepted AspectofInsight instead says actual falling dynamic maxima use accepted clamp rule.','A: expressly scoped Eye-only conserved reserve with actual pool identity/source-qualified permanent loss and no refill into reserved capacity. B: ordinary cap-clamp loss and no reserve.','Request explicit decision and complete algorithm; no generic new capacity law is preapproved. HP remains the reviewed downward clamp, never reserved. Define nested Eye applications, multiple bonuses, gain/refund at below-cap total, partial restoration and real permanent loss. Only a truly independent remaining permission may spend accessible units; suppressed class engines cannot spend their own reserve.'),
('EYE1-Q11',IDS,'Finite storage records such as Mirrorsage Echo slots, prepared matrices, Druid reserve snapshots, Tinker items and RevelationCharges are unlike interchangeable RP.','A: preserve actual records and source-specific initialization/recovery clocks; suppress permissions, never refill/recreate contents or silently apply a fungible12unit example to every storage system. B: pool all records under a universal reserve.','Recommend A. A capacity loss needs a declared stable inaccessible record selection if applicable, preserving item/echo identity, provenance and first-use history. An unacquired feature is not initialized on return; cooldown elapsed progress may continue, but missed triggered recoveries remain lost. Actual restoration grants no rest or encounter-start floor.'),
('EYE1-Q12',IDS,'Multiple Eye applications, local antimagic clipping and independent suppression of target’s underlying features create layered dependencies.','A: each Eye original endpoint persists; any surviving applicable Eye keeps its covered mechanics suppressed; suppressing Eye restores only otherwise eligible still-live outputs. B: last cleanup restores all regardless of remaining causes.','Recommend A with exact dispel/field-locus rules and explicit owner/dependent output propagation. A field covering the Eye target may suppress Eye and some separately magical underlying powers simultaneously; no unconditional return of everything. Preserve same-source history and no renewed hard-control admission. All75domain/runtime/human/balance/cosmology gates remain separate.'),
('EYE1-Q13',IDS,'Full cross-class engine suppression is not implemented, and two original examples are abstract capacity arithmetic.','A: give a source-linked classification/exception matrix and require concrete current cases for representative distinct dependency types after actual decisions. B: mark all17classes tested based on2generic examples.','Recommend A. Minimum cases should address Oracle protectedCurse, actual mundane survivingAction, Wizard independent oldspell/Readycast, Druid formbody/meld/conflict, remote dependentHP, actual resourcebonus, recordstorage and nested suppression. Use complete actual acquisitions/actors and present source status, including proposed-versus-reviewed distinction; no fabricated capacity feature or CR profile.')
]
